      "artist": "No machine-readable author provided. Cla68 assumed (based on copyright claims).",
      "description": "Route of approach of Mikawa's ships for the Battle of Savo Island, August 7-8, 1942.  Aoba, Kako, Kinugasa, and Furutaka departed Kavieng (upper left) and joined Chokai, Tenryu, Yubari, and Yunagi between Rabaul and Cape St. George at sunset on August 7 (\"A\").  The force paused off Kieta, Bougainville from dawn until noon, August 8 (\"B\") and then proceeded down The Slot towards Savo Island and Guadalcanal, sighting the U.S. destroyer Blue at 00:54 on August 9 (\"C\").  Source:  Morison, Struggle for Guadalcanal, p. 21.\n\nModification of public domain image RabaulStratArea.jpg by cla68 on August 31, 2006.",
